The Delaware County Bar Association is seeking a new Executive Director. The Association is a 900 \-member volunteer organization that serves its member attorneys, collaborates with the local judiciary, and interacts with the state bar association and other local associations.

The Executive Director of the Delaware County Bar Association is the Association’s Chief Administrative Officer responsible for leading and managing the affairs of the Association and implementing its policies and procedures for the benefit of the membership.

**RESPONSIBILITIES AND DUTIES**

The Executive Director reports to the Board of Directors, which oversees the operations and finances of the Association, periodically reviews and amends the Association By\-Laws, and establishes the Association’s goals and objectives. The Executive Director works in cooperation with the Board of Directors to implement its policies and directives, as follows:

· Maintain frequent communications with the Board of Directors and its Executive Committee concerning issues that affect the Association and its members;

· Attend all Executive Committee Meetings and Board Meetings;

· Provide the Executive Committee and Board with monthly financial and activity reports, including monthly Profit \& Loss Reports;

· Exercise managerial oversight and supervision of all Association staff;

· Coordinate and assist with the operation of all Association programs, committees, and sections; and

· Perform all other tasks or responsibilities that may be delegated by the Executive Committee or Board of Directors, from time to time.

As the Chief Administrative Office of the Association, the Executive Director must be able to:

· Understand and keep current on changes affecting the legal profession to ensure that the operations of the Association remain relevant and valuable to its membership;

· Possess strong decision\-making skills, and be able to manage collaborative decision making with the Executive Board, Board of Directors, and Association staff;

· Develop and communicate clear goals and objectives;

· Effectively represent the Association at the local, state, and national level with other professional bar associations or organizations;

· Maintain a positive image for the Association in the community;

· Execute the mission and goals of the Association to provide quality member services;

· Understand relevant employment/labor laws;

· Understand the various Association functions and activities, including (but not limited to): the Legal Journal, Lawyer Referral Service, CLE Programming, marketing, accounting / bookkeeping, and member communications / publications;

· Ensure effective and efficient day\-to\-day operations of the Association;

· Maintain accurate records of activities of the Association;

· Gain familiarity and proficiency with the technology and IT services used by the Association;

· Interact with the various Association Sections and Committees, including maintaining communication with Section and Committee leadership, and providing assistance when solicited or appropriate;

· Work with the local judiciary and when appropriate, serve as a liaison between the local Bench and Association leadership;

· Serve as the Executive Director of the Delaware County Bar Foundation;

· Be responsible for the financial oversight of the Association;

· Work with the Association’s Budget and Finance Committee to develop an annual budget;

· Possess familiarity with the Association’s accounting software;

· Meet regularly with the Association’s accounting firm regarding oversight of Association finances;

· Understand and assist with the preparation and submission of the Association’s annual IRS 990 tax filings;

· Review monthly bank and investment statements;

· Work closely with the Treasurer of the Association with regard to the Association’s finances, banking, and investments;

· Solicit sponsorships to support Association programs and events;

· Monitor funding/grant opportunities for 501(c)(6\) organizations and apply for those grants when appropriate or when directed;

· Identify and secure alternative sources of revenue for the Association;

· Identify and develop new strategies for membership expansion, retention, and engagement;

· Communicate and expand awareness of member benefits offered by the Association;

· Maintain frequent communication with Association membership;

· Participate in Association and member activities and events; and

· Work closely with the Membership/Orientation Committee.

Further, the Executive Director should be able to:

· Evaluate and implement technology that improves operations, communications, member services and efficiency;

· Identify outdated processes;

· Digitize or streamline workflows;

· Maintain organizational continuity when systems or institutional knowledge are outdated;

· Maintain relationships with county government, elected officials, municipal leaders, nonprofit organizations, law schools and other community institutions;

· Represent DCBA at external meetings and events;

· Identify opportunities for partnerships and visibility;

· Personally cultivate relationships with banks, insurance providers, technology companies, investigators, financial advisors and other legal\-industry vendors;

· Create sponsorship packages, negotiate benefits, and ensure sponsor deliverables are fulfilled;

· Write sponsor advertising copy and integrate sponsors into events, publications, podcasts and other programming;

· Manage the Bar Association's physical facility, including maintenance needs, vendors, improvements and unexpected building issues;

· Develop funding strategies for capital/maintenance expenses and ensure the building remains functional for members, staff and events.

**DESIRED QUALIFICATIONS**

* B.A. or B.S. from an accredited college or university
* Five or more years of experience in Association or non\-profit management
* Strong inter\-personal and communication skills
